            <ArticleTitle>[Generalized brain edema and cerebral infarct in ergotamine abuse: imaging by computerized tomography, magnetic resonance tomography and angiography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>107-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abuse of ergotamine can release a generalised brain edema and brain infarctions. This can be visualized by CT, MR and angiography. The reason, however, can only be found in the patients history.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
